With `--decreases-orders`, a checked user implementation of `Wfo.aha` may apply its total chain
parameter in the well-foundedness proof of an order used in modular-termination bounds. Ordinary
calls still account for their actual chain argument, and the witness's postcondition and termination
remain checked. Passing chains to ordinary helper parameters remains subject to the existing
closed-code rules. The option remains disabled by default.
